>
> Is it possible to see a clover, even if your luck is already maxed out?

No.  In the code it compares your luck before the prayer to your
luck after the prayer and only reports a clover if your luck increased.

>  How much does seeing a clover actually affect your luck, anyhow?

Have luck decrease, no clover.  Have 0 change, no clover.  Have
1 or more increase, yes clover.

Your worst case in a single sac-fest is about 20 clovers.  Luck can
range from -13 to +13 but a luckstone does a +/- bias of 3 so the
ranges are -13 to +7 if carrying a cursed luckstone, -10 to +10 if
not carrying a luckstone, -7 to +13 if carrying an uncursed or
blessed luckstone.

It is possible to hit max with seeing fewer than 10 clovers, or
possible for them to occur 20 times.

I think you're missing something with luckstones.  Maybe you
killed friendly humans for -1 each?  I once wiped out the watch
while carrying an uncursed luckstone then got killed by wargs
because I had become so unlucky I could not hit them any more.

Or you are carrying an item that is counting as a cursed luckstone
and your luck is drifting down between sac fests.

Or you put it in a bag between sac fests and forgot.



